Job Postings API Endpoints Summary:
    1. Create a Job Post
    Endpoint: POST /api/jobs/
    Purpose: Allows a recruiter to create a new job posting. The recruiter field is automatically set to the logged-in user.
    Permissions: IsRecruiterOrAdmin (Only users with the "recruiter" role can create).
    Example Request:
        POST /api/jobs/
        Content-Type: application/json
        Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>

        {
    "title": "Backend Engineer",
    "description": "Seeking a skilled Backend Engineer to develop and maintain robust server-side applications.",
    "skills": [
        "Python",
        "Django",
        "SQL",
        "REST APIs",
        "Git"
    ],
    "status": "draft"
}
    Example Response (201 Created): {
    "id": 101,
    "title": "Backend Engineer",
    "description": "Seeking a skilled Backend Engineer to develop and maintain robust server-side applications.",
    "skills": [
        "Python",
        "Django",
        "SQL",
        "REST APIs",
        "Git"
    ],
    "status": "draft",
    "opened_at": null,
    "closed_at": null,
    "recruiter": 5,
    "recruiter_username": "recruiter_alice",
    "created_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z"
}
2. List All Job Posts
Endpoint: GET /api/jobs/
Purpose: Retrieves a list of all job postings. Can be filtered by recruiter ID or status.
Permissions: IsRecruiterOrAdmin (Admins see all jobs; Recruiters typically see their own jobs, or all 'open' jobs depending on get_queryset logic).
Example Request (No Filters):
    GET /api/jobs/
    Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>
Example Request (Filtered by Status):
    GET /api/jobs/?status=open
    Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>
Example Response (200 OK - filtered list): [
    {
        "id": 101,
        "title": "Backend Engineer",
        "description": "Seeking a skilled Backend Engineer to develop and maintain robust server-side applications.",
        "skills": [
            "Python",
            "Django",
            "SQL",
            "REST APIs",
            "Git"
        ],
        "status": "draft",
        "opened_at": null,
        "closed_at": null,
        "recruiter": 5,
        "recruiter_username": "recruiter_alice",
        "created_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z"
    }
]
3. Retrieve a Specific Job Post
    Endpoint: GET /api/jobs/<id>/
    Purpose: Fetches details for a single job posting by its ID.
    Permissions: IsOwnerOrAdmin (Admins can view any job; Recruiters can view their own jobs).
    Example Request:
        GET /api/jobs/101/
        Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>
    Example Response (200 OK): {
    "id": 101,
    "title": "Backend Engineer",
    "description": "Seeking a skilled Backend Engineer to develop and maintain robust server-side applications.",
    "skills": [
        "Python",
        "Django",
        "SQL",
        "REST APIs",
        "Git"
    ],
    "status": "draft",
    "opened_at": null,
    "closed_at": null,
    "recruiter": 5,
    "recruiter_username": "recruiter_alice",
    "created_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z"
}
4. Update a Job Post (Partial Update)
Endpoint: PATCH /api/jobs/<id>/
Purpose: Allows the owner recruiter or an admin to partially update fields of a job posting.
Permissions: IsOwnerOrAdmin (Only the recruiter who created the job or an admin can update).
Example Request:
    PATCH /api/jobs/101/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>

{
    "status": "open",
    "skills": [
        "Python",
        "Django",
        "SQL",
        "REST APIs",
        "Git",
        "Docker"
    ]
}
Example Response (200 OK): {
    "id": 101,
    "title": "Backend Engineer",
    "description": "Seeking a skilled Backend Engineer to develop and maintain robust server-side applications.",
    "skills": [
        "Python",
        "Django",
        "SQL",
        "REST APIs",
        "Git",
        "Docker"
    ],
    "status": "open",
    "opened_at": "2023-10-27T15:30:00.000000Z", // Automatically updated
    "closed_at": null,
    "recruiter": 5,
    "recruiter_username": "recruiter_alice",
    "created_at": "2023-10-27T15:00:00.000000Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-27T15:30:00.000000Z" // Automatically updated
}
5. Delete a Job Post
Endpoint: DELETE /api/jobs/<id>/
Purpose: Deletes a job posting by its ID.
Permissions: IsOwnerOrAdmin (Only the recruiter who created the job or an admin can delete).
Example Request:
    DELETE /api/jobs/101/
    Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>
Example Response (204 No Content):
(No response body)
6. Get AI Job Suggestions
Endpoint: POST /api/jobs/suggest-description/
Purpose: Generates a suggested job description and required skills based on a provided job title using the AI integration.
Permissions: IsRecruiterOrAdmin (Only users with the "recruiter" role or admins can access).
Example Request:
    POST /api/jobs/suggest-description/
    Content-Type: application/json
    Authorization: Bearer <your_token_or_session>

    {
    "title": "Cloud Solutions Architect"
}
Example Response (200 OK): {
    "description": "We are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Cloud Solutions Architect to design, implement, and manage scalable cloud infrastructure. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in cloud platforms and a strong understanding of enterprise architecture principles.",
    "skills": [
        "AWS",
        "Azure",
        "Google Cloud",
        "Cloud Architecture",
        "Microservices",
        "Networking",
        "Security",
        "DevOps"
    ]
}